Jenkins is an automation server used mainly for CI/CD.
It helps build, test, and deploy applications automatically.
Jenkins can automatically run jobs when developers push code.
It can connect with Git/GitHub to get source code.
A Jenkins Pipeline defines the steps of the CI/CD process.
Jenkinsfile contains the pipeline configuration as code.
Jenkins can run automated tests after building the application.
It can build Docker images and push them to a container registry.
Jenkins can deploy applications to platforms like AWS, Kubernetes, and servers.
Jenkins helps teams save time, reduce manual work, and deliver software faster
